---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/demo.css';
import Shamir from '../../components/demos/Shamir.astro';

// The written explanation lived here for about an hour on 2026-07-30, when the ladder
// merge had nowhere else to put it. It now has somewhere: /learn/beyond-the-ladder, a
// 102 lesson covering BIP-85 and Shamir together. The lesson explains, the demo shows — so
// this page is the demo plus its caveat, and it links back to the lesson.
---
<Base
  title="Split a secret into shares — the Shamir math behind SLIP-39 · BitcoinKeys.guide"
  description="An interactive demonstration of Shamir's Secret Sharing: split a throwaway secret into five shares where any three rebuild it and any two reveal nothing. The real math behind SLIP-39 seed backups, running in your browser."
  verified="2026-07-30"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive demo · try it yourself</p>
    <h1>Split a secret into <span class="accent">shares</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">
      What if you could cut a backup into five pieces, hand them to five people, and know that <strong>any three</strong> together
      can rebuild it — but <strong>any two</strong> reveal literally nothing? That's <strong>Shamir's Secret Sharing</strong>,
      the math behind <strong>SLIP-39</strong> seed backups. Split a throwaway secret below and try it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <Shamir />
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="label">The honest caveat</span>
      <p style="margin:0">Splitting adds moving parts: more pieces to track, and a wrong threshold can lock <em>you</em> out. Most people are
        better served by a simple, well-guarded seed or <a href="/learn/ladder#rung-3">multisig</a> first. Shamir/SLIP-39 shines when you
        specifically want a <em>backup</em> spread across places without any one being enough.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/learn/beyond-the-ladder">← Read the lesson on Shamir</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/demos/multisig">Multisig vs. this →</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/demos">All demos →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.65rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .btn.ghost:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
</style>

